7:13:36 AM [express] POST /api/ai/chat 200 in 58401ms :: {"response":"Here's a sample Indian diet plan focusing on weight loss:\n\n**Breakfast (approx. 300 kcal):**\n\n*   **Idli with sambar and coconut chutney:** Opt for steamed idlis rather than fried ones. Limit sambar quantity by controlling its thickness. Coconut chutney use sparingly.\n*   **Ragi Dosa:** Ragi dosa is healthier option compared to white dosas. Have it plain or with minimal vegetable filling.\n*   **Upma:** Made with ragi flour or millet flakes. Include lots of veggies.\n\n**Snack (mid morning approx. 100kcal):**\n\n*   A handful of almonds / walnuts (about 15-20 nuts)\n*   Cucumber slices with hummus\n\n**Lunch (approx. 400 kcal):**\n\n*   **Dal Makhani (small serving):** Reduce oil usage during preparation.\n*   **Brown Rice:** Replace white rice with brown rice.\n*   **Vegetable Curry:** Choose low-fat options like stir-fried vegetables cooked in less oil.\n*   **Salad:** Side salad with light dressing.\n\n**Evening Snacks (approx. 100 kcal):**\n\n*   Fruit smoothie (made with fruit, yoghurt and little bit of milk)\n*   Green tea with a few dry fruits\n\n**Dinner (approx. 300 kcal):**\n\n*   **Chicken Soup:** Light broth soup with chicken pieces and vegetables.\n*   **Stir fry:** Non oily stir fries prepared with mixed vegetables.\n\n**Foods to avoid:**\n\n*   Fried snacks (pakoras, samosas, vada pav)\n*   Sugary drinks (colas, juices)\n*   Excessive sweets (barfi, gulab jamun)\n*   Processed foods (packaged biscuits, chips)\n*   High fat dairy products (full cream paneer, ghee heavy curries)\n\n**Reasoning:**\n\nThis plan emphasizes whole grains, lean protein sources, fresh vegetables, and limited unhealthy fats. Portion control is key across all meals. Avoiding processed foods minimizes added sugars and unhealthy ingredients often found in packaged goods. Focusing on home cooking allows better control over ingredient quality and seasoning methods. Regular consumption of these foods combined with consistent exercise leads to sustainable weight reduction.\n\n[MACROS: Protein 60%, Carbs 30%, Fat 10%]","followUpQuestions":[]}
